    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d195">

                <pb facs="0244" n="236" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg236"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/8407: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Then in France, to the Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">St.
                                Jean de Luz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-29T13:00:00+01:00">August 29, 1938—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 29—9:54 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>519. I have just learned from most reliable quarters, identified in despatch
                    going out today,<anchor n="90" xml:id="d195-f1"/> that the rigid closing of
                    frontier due to serious dissensions across the border, involving among other
                    things <pb facs="0245" n="237" xml:id="pg237"/> a conflict between Franco and
                    General Anido, Minister of Interior and hailed as “the strong man”. Franco plans
                    to dismiss Anido and serious trouble feared. Defeatist note common in San
                    Sebastian, not unheard even at Burgos, but suppressed at Saragossa and near the
                    front. Even Marquis de Rialp<anchor n="91" xml:id="d195-f2"/> unable to cross
                    border Saturday to keep engagement with me. Most serious conflict apparently
                    between Franco’s group and Falangists.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d195-f1" n="90" xml:id="d195-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d195-f2" n="91" xml:id="d195-f2-content">
                <p>Representing Franco in arrangements with Ambassador Bowers for the exchange of
                    prisoners. See <ref target="#pg285">pp. 285</ref>–<ref target="#pg345">345</ref>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">passim</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
